# Next.js Guardrails

Architecture:
- App Router structure with explicit route boundaries
- default to Server Components
- use Client Components only when interactivity requires it

Implementation discipline:
- minimize `'use client'` scope
- keep data-fetching server-side when feasible
- keep route/module naming consistent and predictable
- keep error/loading states explicit on async boundaries

Quality checks:
- avoid unnecessary client-side state/effect for server-solvable concerns
- keep API consumption typed and resilient
